(6478474, 962175, 54645, '<td valign="top">I really enjoyed this image, well, I still do! I was reading <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=61396" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mitalapo</a>''s comment, which is actually quite accurate depending on perspective...it got me thinking...yes, the interpretation is not a story, but, for me, more of an emotional response to a seascape...if a viewer sticks around long enough to feel that emotion, eventually a story well develop even if it has nothing to do with the beach/ocean/etc. Likely more to do with something in their immediate life experience, yeah? I think you mostly hit that mark, which, I hope, is why it did so well...specifically it surrounds the shell. My initial response...why is that there? Does it belong? Ultimately it made me feel a bit lonely and out of place...maybe left behind.  If you can evoke a response like that, then I personally feel the photograph is a success. I was too tired to write this out when I commented originally, so you got my clinical comment. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-07-22 01:04:03.</i></td>', 'I really enjoyed this image, well, I still do! I was reading  mitalapo''s comment, which is actually quite accurate depending on perspective...it got me thinking...yes, the interpretation is not a story, but, for me, more of an emotional response to a seascape...if a viewer sticks around long enough to feel that emotion, eventually a story well develop even if it has nothing to do with the beach/ocean/etc. Likely more to do with something in their immediate life experience, yeah? I think you mostly hit that mark, which, I hope, is why it did so well...specifically it surrounds the shell. My initial response...why is that there? Does it belong? Ultimately it made me feel a bit lonely and out of place...maybe left behind.  If you can evoke a response like that, then I personally feel the photograph is a success. I was too tired to write this out when I commented originally, so you got my clinical comment. :)', '2011-07-22 01:57:37.000000', '2011-07-22 02:04:03.000000', 0),
