(6478769, 962140, 134665, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by senor_kasper:</b></div><hr/><i> You won''t be dq''d if you have the un-edited jpg. Just don''t do anything to it but send it untouched to the SC. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Added some clarification, I captured in RAW and then converted to JPEG and saved the file.  I had the RAW file and JPEG file at one point, one was on my hard drive and the other on the external hard drive.  I have the JPEG after the conversion from RAW to JPEG (without any further edits), but I don''t'' think this will work after reading the rules.  Let me know if I''m reading this wrong - thank you for commenting!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-07-22 10:37:25.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by senor_kasper: You won''t be dq''d if you have the un-edited jpg. Just don''t do anything to it but send it untouched to the SC.   Added some clarification, I captured in RAW and then converted to JPEG and saved the file.  I had the RAW file and JPEG file at one point, one was on my hard drive and the other on the external hard drive.  I have the JPEG after the conversion from RAW to JPEG (without any further edits), but I don''t'' think this will work after reading the rules.  Let me know if I''m reading this wrong - thank you for commenting!', '2011-07-22 11:36:51.000000', '2011-07-22 11:37:25.000000', 0),
